{
  "summary": "This experiment replaced the PCA (n2000) RNA encoder with a learned scVI encoder (n200) in the multimodal, single-profile, ResNet-50, concat-fusion setting, constituting a single-variable change from llm_summary_002. The configuration achieved a validation accuracy of 0.536 (F1 0.516), exceeding both the PCA-based multimodal baseline (0.527, F1 0.510) and the RNA-only scVI result (0.520, F1 0.498), suggesting that the scVI encoder gain is at least partially additive with the multimodal image contribution. It remains uncertain whether the modest ~0.9% improvement over the PCA multimodal configuration is stable across runs, whether the gain is driven by the learned representation or the reduced dimensionality (200 vs. 2000), and whether this advantage persists under alternative fusion strategies or multiprofile settings."
}

